-- title:
--   Independent tangent directions give distinct contracted branch primes
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$, a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\neq q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $q\ell$, let $\zeta\in L$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity and $\xi\in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity.
--
--   The function field. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ with $K=\mathtt{ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange}\,L\bigl(\mathtt{ModularCurve.xHFunctionField}\,((q\ell)^2M')\,(\mathtt{ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH}\,(q\ell)\,M')\bigr)$, i.e. $K$ is the $L$-subfield of $L((t))$ generated by the coefficientwise image (under $\mathtt{ModularCurve.coeffEmb}\,L$, the map induced by $\mathbb{Q}\to L$) of the function field of the modular curve of level $N_0=(q\ell)^2M'$ attached to the subgroup $\mathtt{levelH}\,(q\ell)\,M'\le(\mathbb{Z}/N_0)^\times$, the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$.
--
--   The base ring and the coordinate. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring which is an $L$-algebra with $L$ as its fraction ring, such that $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A\to L$, and let $\varpi\in A$ generate the maximal ideal; $A$ acts on $K$ compatibly with $L$. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent image $\mathtt{coeffEmb}\,L\,\mathtt{ModularCurve.jq}$, the $q$-expansion $t^{-1}+\dots$ of the modular $j$-function.
--
--   The integral model. Write $X=\mathtt{AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel}\,A\,K\,j$, the scheme obtained by gluing (as a pushout of the two chart morphisms) the spectra of the two $A$-subalgebras of $K$ attached to $j$ and to its inverse; here $\mathtt{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j$ is the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, and $\mathtt{jChartFin}$ is $j$ viewed inside it. Let $z$ be a point of $X$, and let $\varpi z$ be the element of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ obtained as the germ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under the structure morphism $\mathtt{toBase}\,A\,K\,j : X\to\operatorname{Spec}A$ on global sections; it is assumed that $\varpi z$ lies in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$. Let $y$ be a point of $\mathtt{XFin}\,A\,K\,j=\operatorname{Spec}(\mathtt{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j)$ with $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}(y)=z$.
--
--   Supersingularity at $y$ (hypothesis `hss`). For every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi:\mathtt{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j\to\Omega$ with kernel the prime $y$, the value $\varphi(\mathtt{jChartFin})$ lies in $\mathtt{ModularCurve.ssJSet}\,q\,\Omega$, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero point killed by $q$.
--
--   The Drinfeld chart witness. Let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation ring, $\sigma:A\to W$ a ring homomorphism with $\sigma\varpi$ generating the maximal ideal of $W$, and let $f,u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and
--   $$f-\bigl(X_0X_1^{\,q}-X_0^{\,q}X_1\bigr)\in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2},$$
--   the subtracted series being $\mathtt{DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm}\,q\,W$. Let
--   $$e:\widehat{\mathcal{O}_{X,z}}\;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\;S:=W[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma\varpi)\,v-f\,u\bigr)$$
--   be a ring isomorphism from the completion of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ along its maximal ideal. Throughout, $\mathrm{toC}$ denotes the completion map $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}\to\widehat{\mathcal{O}_{X,z}}$, $\mathrm{mkS}$ the quotient map $W[[X_0,X_1]]\to S$, and $\mathrm{germ}_Y$ the canonical homomorphism $\mathtt{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j\to\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ obtained from the global-sections identification of the finite chart followed by the germ at $z$.
--
--   Riders on the witness (hypothesis `hW`, two clauses). First, compatibility on constants: for every $a\in A$ the element $e(\mathrm{toC}(\text{germ of }a))$ equals $\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma a))$. Second, linearisation of level automorphisms: for every $\gamma\in SL_2(\mathbb{Z})$ lying in $\Gamma_0(M')$, every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying $\mathtt{ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt}\,L\,(q\ell)\,\xi\,(q\ell)\,((q\ell)^2M')\,(\mathtt{levelH}\,(q\ell)\,M')\,\gamma^{-1}\,K\,\tau$ — that is, $\tau$ implements, on all quotients of $q$-expansions of weight-$k$ modular forms for the level-$N_0$ group attached to $\mathtt{levelH}\,(q\ell)\,M'$ with integral $q$-expansions, the substitution by the scaled conjugate of $\gamma^{-1}$, for every embedding $\iota:L\to\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\xi=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$ — and every proof that $\tau$ maps $\mathtt{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j$ into itself, if the restriction of $\tau$ to that chart algebra is congruent to the identity modulo the prime $y$, then there exist a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c\in W$ and a matrix $M\in M_2(W)$ such that: $\theta$ intertwines the two maps $\mathtt{chartAlgFin}\to S$, namely $\theta(e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germ}_Y a)))=e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germ}_Y(\tau a)))$ for all $a$; $\theta$ fixes $\mathrm{mkS}(C w)$ for all $w\in W$; for each index $j'$, $\theta(\mathrm{mkS}(X_{j'}))-\mathrm{mkS}\bigl(\sum_{i}C(M_{ij'})X_i\bigr)$ lies in the square of the ideal generated by $\mathrm{mkS}(X_0),\mathrm{mkS}(X_1)$; $c^{q+1}-1$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W$; $M_{ij'}-c\,\gamma_{ij'}$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W$ for all $i,j'$; if $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$ then $c-1$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W$; and if $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity on $K$ then $c-1$ does not lie in the maximal ideal of $W$.
--
--   Witness-free riders (hypothesis `hEQ`, two clauses). First, every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying the above level condition for some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ maps $\mathtt{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j$ into itself. Second, if moreover $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$, then the restriction of such a $\tau$ to the chart algebra is congruent to the identity modulo the prime $y$.
--
--   Conclusion. Assume that the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ possesses two prime ideals $Q_1\neq Q_2$, both containing $\varpi z$ and neither maximal. Then for all integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and all prime ideals $P_1,P_2$ of $S$ such that for each $i$ at least one of $\mathrm{mkS}(X_0),\mathrm{mkS}(X_1)$ avoids $P_i$, such that $\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma\varpi))\in P_1$ and $\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma\varpi))\in P_2$, such that for each $i$ there is $h_i\in (X_0,X_1)^2$ with $\mathrm{mkS}\bigl(C(a_i)X_0+C(b_i)X_1+h_i\bigr)\in P_i$ (the images of $a_i,b_i$ in $W$ being taken via $\mathbb{Z}\to W$), and such that $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$, the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ along the composite of $\mathrm{toC}$ with $e$ are distinct ideals of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$:
--   $$\mathrm{comap}\,(e\circ\mathrm{toC})\,P_1\;\neq\;\mathrm{comap}\,(e\circ\mathrm{toC})\,P_2.$$
--
--   At a supersingular point $z$ of the integral model the complete local ring is a Drinfeld-type chart $W[[X_0,X_1]]/(\sigma\varpi v-fu)$ with $q+1$ formal branches over the special fibre, indexed by the tangent directions $a X_0+bX_1$ modulo $q$; the statement says that, once the stalk is known to have at least two distinct non-maximal primes over $\varpi$, branches whose tangent directions are independent modulo $q$ already lie on distinct global components. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.isDiscreteValuationRing_stalk_quotient_of_mem_of_not_isMaximal_of_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.isDiscreteValuationRing_stalk_quotient_of_mem_of_not_isMaximal_of_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel), where regularity of the components of the special fibre at $z$ is deduced.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_AuxLevel_comap_ne_comap_of_branchPrime_of_exists_ne_of_drinfeldChartWitness_riders_twoChartIntegralModel.lean

